[0.103212, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m Based on my analysis of both streamers' songlists and configurations, here are \u001b[1m2 interesting facts\u001b[22m comparing\r\n  vu_vu and belleune:\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m🎵 Catalog Size & Activity Contrast\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mvu_vu\u001b[22m: 266 songs, but \u001b[1m0 songs have ever been played\u001b[22m (all show \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mtimesPlayed: 0\u001b[39m)\r\n  \u001b[1mbelleune\u001b[22m: 545 songs (2x more!), with high engagement (top songs played 50+ times)\r\n\r\n  This reveals a stark difference: vu_vu appears to have a mostly unused catalog while belleune has an active,\r\n  frequently-played repertoire that's more than twice the size.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m🎹 Musical Specialization & Organization\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mvu_vu\u001b[22m: Minimal organization with only 1 attribute category (\"music\") for subscribers only\r\n  \u001b[1mbelleune\u001b[22m: Highly organized with \u001b[1m12 detailed mood/genre categories\u001b[22m including:\r\n  - \"Jazz 👐🏼\" (priority-based)\r\n  - \"Originals 🔔🌙\", \"Loops "]
[0.000011, "o", "🔁\", \"Favs 🥰\"\r\n  - \"Chill 🍸\", \"Sad vibes 😢\", \"Good vibes 😎\"\r\n  - \"Love ❤️\", \"Instrumental 🎹\" (subscriber-only)\r\n  - \"Disney 🏰\", \"Movies, TV & Games\", \"Ukulele\"\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\n  The comparison reveals two completely different streaming approaches: vu_vu has a basic setup with unused\r\n  songs, while belleune runs a sophisticated music curation system with emotional/mood-based organization and\r\n  active community engagement. This suggests belleune is likely a music-focused streamer with a dedicated\r\n  audience, while vu_vu may be more experimental or have different streaming priorities.\r\n  \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m─────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  The data also shows belleune has much more sophisticated queue management (amount-based pri"]
[0.000017, "o", "oritization,\r\n  strict cooldowns) compared to vu_vu's simpler FIFO approach, further highlighting their different streaming\r\n  philosophies.\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✻\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;119;87mSlithering… \u001b[39m\u001b[2m(esc to interrupt · 42s · ↓\u001b[22m \u001b[2m1.4k tokens)\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m> \u001b[22m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
