[0.00141, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2J\u001b[3J\u001b[H\r\n\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m▗\u001b[48;2;215;119;87m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ▗   ▖ \u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m▖\u001b[39m  \u001b[1mClaude Code\u001b[22m \u001b[2mv2.0.14\u001b[22m\r\n \u001b[48;2;215;119;87m       \u001b[49m   \u001b[2mglm-4.6 · API Usage Billing\u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;215;119;87m▘▘ ▝▝\u001b[39m    \u001b[2m/Users/vuvu-mbp/Developer/mcp/streamersonglist-mcp\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m> use the streamersonglist-mcp to find out what songs vu_vu has on his queue \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m I'll help you find out what songs vu_vu has on their queue using the streamersonglist-mcp. Let me first check\r\n   if the MCP server is available and then use the getQueue tool to retrieve the current queue information.\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;107;128m⏺\u001b[39m \u001b[1mlistMcpResources\u001b[22m(List MCP resources from server \"streamersonglist-mcp\")\r\n  ⎿  \u001b[38;2;255;107;128mError: Server \"streamersonglist-mcp\" not found. Available servers: voicemode, ide\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m I see that the streamersonglist-mcp server isn't currently "]
[0.00002, "o", "available as an MCP resource. Let me check if I\r\n  can run it directly from the current directory to access the queue information.\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m⏺\u001b[39m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[22m(npm start)\r\n  ⎿  \u001b[2mRunning in the background (down arrow to manage)\u001b[22m\u001b(B\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m⏺\u001b[39m \u001b[1mBashOutput\u001b[22m(Reading shell output)\r\n  ⎿  > streamersonglist-mcp@1.3.1 start          \u001b(B\r\n     > node src/server.js\r\n  ⎿  \u001b[38;2;255;107;128mStreamerSongList MCP Server running on stdio\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m I notice the server started but then completed. Let me try a different approach - I'll make a direct API call\r\n   to the StreamerSongList API to get vu_vu's queue information, since this is what the MCP server would do\r\n  anyway.\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m⏺\u001b[39m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[22m(curl -s \"https://api.streamersonglist.com/v1/streamers/vu_vu/queue\" | jq '.')\r\n  ⎿  {                              \u001b(B\r\n       \"list\": [\r\n         {\r\n     \u001b[2m… +160 lines (ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[3"]
[0.000022, "o", "9m Perfect! I was able to retrieve vu_vu's current queue from the StreamerSongList API. Here's what I found:\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mvu_vu's Current Queue\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mTotal songs in queue:\u001b[22m 5 songs\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2mQueue Details:\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  1. \u001b[1mPosition 1:\u001b[22m \"NOT A REAL SONG\" by KEKYou (added June 12, 2023)\r\n  2. \u001b[1mPosition 2:\u001b[22m \"NOT A REAL SONG\" by KEKYou (added June 12, 2023)\r\n  3. \u001b[1mPosition 3:\u001b[22m \"NOT A REAL SONG\" by KEKYou (added June 12, 2023)\r\n  4. \u001b[1mPosition 4:\u001b[22m \"NOT A REAL SONG\" by KEKYou (added June 12, 2023)\r\n  5. \u001b[1mPosition 5:\u001b[22m \"Baka Mitai\" by Yakuza OST (added October 11, 2025) - \u001b[3mRecently requested by vu_vu\u001b[23m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2mAdditional Info:\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  - \u001b[1mSongs played today:\u001b[22m 0\r\n  - \u001b[1mMost recent activity:\u001b[22m \"Baka Mitai\" was requested by vu_vu and is currently in chat\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\n  The API shows that most of the queue appears to be fille"]
[0.000064, "o", "d with placeholder/test songs (\"NOT A REAL SONG\" by\r\n  KEKYou) from June 2023, with only one recent legitimate song request. This suggests the streamer may have\r\n  been testing their system or these are old queued items that haven't been cleared.\r\n  \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m─────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  The queue data shows that vu_vu has 5 songs currently queued, with the most recent being \"Baka Mitai\" from\r\n  the Yakuza soundtrack, which was actively requested and is currently being highlighted in the chat.\r\n\r\n\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m> compare vu_vu songlist with belleune and tell me 2 interesting facts about it \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m I'll compare the songlists for both streamers and find some interesting differences. Let me retrieve the data\r\n   for both vu_vu and belleune.\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m⏺\u001b[39m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[22m(curl -s \"https://api.streamersonglist.co"]
